Description: avfilter/stereo3d: preserve eye order for interleaved columns
 Select the source column from the input eye order and leave the output
 placement to the selected output layout. Swapping the configured offsets
 as well as the source columns reversed icr packed output. Depending on
 the output enum parity also reversed right-first alternating output.
 .
 Use the actual input order when interleaving columns again, so icl:icr
 exchanges the eyes instead of copying the original column order.
 .
 Add an analytic RGB FATE regression with different markers in each eye.
 Use frame MD5 because the exchanged views have the same Adler checksum.
 The reference is generated from independently packed left and right
 images, and fails on unpatched master.
 .
 Signed-off-by: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
 Assisted-by: gpt-6-astra via Codex
